This is a fantastic UI tweak. Expanding the *active* step into a "pill" shape with the full text inside looks much cleaner and saves vertical space in the grid, while keeping the past/future steps as compact circles.
Here are the **2 exact changes** to implement this inside your JournalAuthorization.jsx file.
### 1. Update the CustomWorkflowIcon Component
We will add an isMini flag and a label property so the icon can automatically stretch into a pill shape to fit the text when it is the active step.
**FIND your CustomWorkflowIcon component (around line 180) and REPLACE it with this:**
```javascript
  const CustomWorkflowIcon = (props) => {
    const { statusFlag, iconLetter, label, isMini } = props;

    // If it's the mini stepper AND it's the currently active step, expand it to show the full name
    const showTextInside = isMini && (statusFlag === 'ACTIVE' || statusFlag === 'ESCALATED');

    const baseStyle = {
      height: 28, 
      borderRadius: 14, // Pill shape
      display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center', justifyContent: 'center',
      zIndex: 2, position: 'relative', // Ensures it stays above the connector line
      color: '#fff', fontSize: '0.75rem', fontWeight: 'bold',
      px: showTextInside ? 1.5 : 0,
      minWidth: showTextInside ? 'auto' : 28,
      width: showTextInside ? 'max-content' : 28,
      whiteSpace: 'nowrap'
    };

    if (statusFlag === 'COMPLETED') {
      return <Box sx={{ ...baseStyle, backgroundColor: 'success.main' }}><CheckIcon sx={{ fontSize: 18 }} /></Box>;
    }
    if (statusFlag === 'REJECTED') {
      return <Box sx={{ ...baseStyle, backgroundColor: 'error.main' }}><CloseIcon sx={{ fontSize: 18 }} /></Box>;
    }
    if (statusFlag === 'ESCALATED') {
      return (
        <Tooltip title="Escalation Time Breached - Attention Required" arrow>
          <Box sx={{ ...baseStyle, backgroundColor: 'warning.main', border: '2px solid #fff3e0' }}>
            {showTextInside ? `${label} ⚠️` : '!'}
          </Box>
        </Tooltip>
      );
    }
    if (statusFlag === 'ACTIVE') {
      return (
        <Box sx={{ ...baseStyle, backgroundColor: 'primary.main', border: '2px solid #e3f2fd' }}>
          {showTextInside ? label : iconLetter}
        </Box>
      );
    }
    
    // PENDING / FUTURE STEPS (Grey)
    return <Box sx={{ ...baseStyle, backgroundColor: '#e2e8f0', color: '#64748b' }}>{iconLetter}</Box>;
  };

```
### 2. Update the DataGrid Mini-Stepper
We need to pass the new isMini and label props into the icon, remove the old label that was rendering below it, and allow the Step container to flexibly resize to fit the new pill width.
**FIND your workflowState column inside the columns array, and REPLACE the <Stepper> block with this:**
```javascript
          <Box sx={{ width: '100%', display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center', justifyContent: 'flex-start', pl: 2, height: '100%' }}>
            <Stepper activeStep={activeStep} alternativeLabel connector={<CustomConnector />} sx={{ width: '100%', mt: 0.5 }}>
              {stepLabels.map((label, index) => {
                const isCompleted = index < activeStep;
                const isCurrent = index === activeStep;
                
                let statusFlag = 'PENDING';
                if (isCompleted) statusFlag = 'COMPLETED';
                if (isCurrent && isRejected) statusFlag = 'REJECTED';
                else if (isCurrent && isEscalated) statusFlag = 'ESCALATED';
                else if (isCurrent) statusFlag = 'ACTIVE';

                return (
                  <Tooltip title={label} key={`${label}-${index}`} arrow>
                    {/* Removed the rigid flex width so it perfectly adjusts to the pill size */}
                    <Step completed={isCompleted} active={isCurrent} sx={{ px: 0, opacity: (isRejected && index > activeStep) ? 0.3 : 1 }}>
                      
                      {/* Pass isMini={true} and the label down to the icon */}
                      <StepLabel StepIconComponent={() => <CustomWorkflowIcon statusFlag={statusFlag} iconLetter={label.charAt(0).toUpperCase()} label={label} isMini={true} />} sx={{ p: 0, m: 0 }}>
                        {/* The Typography label that was here is completely removed because it is now inside the icon! */}
                      </StepLabel>

                    </Step>
                  </Tooltip>
                );
              })}
            </Stepper>
          </Box>

```
**(Note: You do not need to change the Big Stepper inside the view modal. Because we don't pass isMini={true} into the Big Stepper, it will automatically remain as perfectly round circles with the details written below them.)**
